prompt:
Write public/js/toast.js (new file, about 40 lines), a classic script loaded before main.js (STU-UX2: one way to tell the user things). Top-level function, no IIFE.
`function toast(message, opts = {})` with opts { action, onAction, kind = 'info', timeout = 5000 }:
- the stack: document.querySelector('.toast-stack'), or create `<div class="toast-stack" aria-live="polite">` and append it to document.body the first time;
- create a <div class="toast"> with role 'alert' when kind is 'error' and 'status' otherwise, and class toast-error for errors; inside it a <span> with the message as textContent (never innerHTML);
- when opts.action is set, add `<button type="button" class="secondary-btn">` with opts.action as text; its click calls opts.onAction (when given) and then removes the toast;
- append the toast to the stack; when timeout > 0 remove it after timeout milliseconds (only if it is still on the page);
- return the toast element.
Output only the file.
